{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_rule_never_write_neo_tree", "label": "Rule 1 \u2014 never write to the NEO tree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NEO is the input and the only source of truth, so the guard is enforced in core/write.js rather than by convention."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rule_dry_run_default", "label": "Rule 2 \u2014 dry run is the default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A partially converted tree that looks complete is worse than none, so --write is explicit and a blocker stops it unless --force."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rule_finding_not_guess", "label": "Rule 3 \u2014 a rule that cannot decide emits a finding, not a guess", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The whole tool's credibility rests on it: a refusal costs a developer ten minutes; a wrong conversion costs a day and may never be found."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rule_ast_locates_text_edited", "label": "Rule 4 \u2014 the AST locates, the original text is edited by offset", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Regenerating JavaScript from the parse tree reformats every file and drops every comment, leaving nothing to diff against the NEO original."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rule_terminal_boundary", "label": "Rule 5 \u2014 only bin/ and src/report/ may write to a terminal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything else returns data, so adding a UI later is a rendering job rather than a rewrite."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rule_single_applyedits", "label": "Rule 6 \u2014 all passes contribute edits to one applyEdits call", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two transforms claiming the same bytes becomes an error instead of one quietly winning."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_pass_order", "label": "JS pass order (imports \u2192 request \u2192 http \u2192 db \u2192 async)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A pass that moves text must run after the passes that rewrite inside what it moves and must replay those rewrites into the copy (ctx.inlineRewrites); get it wrong and the moved copy silently keeps the old $. idiom."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_rewrite_around_not_over", "label": "Rewrite around a sub-expression, never over it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A pass replacing a whole statement locks every other pass out of its interior, so request.js emits pairs of edits bracketing the argument it keeps."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_phase_intake", "label": "Intake phase", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Units are classified by the extensions inside a folder, never its name, because the corpus has Views/View as distinct folders and .xsodata living in a dozen differently-named folders."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_phase_a_parse", "label": "Phase A \u2014 parse every file into data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_backwards_information_flow", "label": "Backwards information flow (xsodata keys into the CDS proxy)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A CDS proxy's key columns are declared in the .xsodata that projects the view, not in the view itself; emitting while walking would mean either a missing key or a forward reference \u2014 which is why parse and emit are separate phases at all."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_phase_b_resolve_names", "label": "Phase B \u2014 resolve names (the proxies map)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The proxies map is keyed by the NEO id (namespace::filename) because that is the id an .xsodata refers to \u2014 which for 92 views in the corpus is not the scenario id inside the XML."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_phase_c_emit", "label": "Phase C \u2014 emit file text", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": ".xsodata files in the same folder are merged into one service.cds because two services in one folder would otherwise fight over the same file name; CAP service names are global, so colliding names are qualified by the first differing folder segment."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_path_asymmetry", "label": "Path asymmetry \u2014 db/ drops <APP>, srv/lib keeps it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both directions verified against a shipped CF tree and both easy to get wrong; a wrong <APP> silently merges unrelated subtrees, which is why intake refuses to guess it."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_whole_tree_passes", "label": "Whole-tree passes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cross-file awaits and the project shell are impossible to see one file at a time, so they run after everything is emitted; the shell is last because what it declares depends on what the run produced."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_write_phase", "label": "Write phase and the two write guards", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_analysis_emission_split", "label": "Analysis / emission split (db.js vs emitdb.js)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three consumers read the same chain object \u2014 the emitter, the report and the AI tier \u2014 so analysis and emission live in separate files; the emitter never re-derives a column name or a bind order."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_jdbc_chain_object", "label": "JDBC chain object (SQL, binds, columns, reads, gaps)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "resolved is simply 'no gap that is not a note'; deliberate refusals each carry their own code \u2014 run-time SQL, computed bind index, a read where the row no longer exists, a computed getX index, a ResultSet method CAP does not have."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_reparse_gate", "label": "The re-parse gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Output is re-parsed as an ES module and the result refused if it does not load; node --check is not equivalent because it treats a file as a script, where XSJS-isms still pass."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_tier2_has_no_emitter", "label": "Tier 2 has no emitter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tier 1 is byte-identical in both modes, enforced by construction: a model's answer re-enters as an input to Tier 1, which decides; if the statement still does not resolve the answer is discarded and the worst a wrong answer can do is waste a call."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ceiling_rule", "label": "The ceiling rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never ask a model about what Tier 1 can decide, and never about a statement with a second blocker \u2014 the answer would convert nothing. Measure with checks/ceiling.js before building anything for a bucket of refusals; four times it replaced planned work with something smaller and deterministic."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ai_task_rules", "label": "Rules for adding an AI task", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ask for an answer never for code; never ask what Tier 1 can decide; validate something semantic (the SQL grammar overrules the model \u2014 a hole after FROM cannot be a bind parameter, a hole after = cannot be an identifier); 'unknown' is a real answer, distinct from never having asked."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ai_classified_marker", "label": "AI-CLASSIFIED marker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything a model decided is marked in the emitted file, not only in the report \u2014 the report is not there when someone reads the code later."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_finding_levels", "label": "Finding levels \u2014 note / warning / blocked", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Findings are as much the deliverable as the code; a finding's `fix` field tells the developer what to change in NEO so the next run converts it, which is the difference between a report and a to-do list."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_verify_sweep", "label": "The verify sweep (ten steps, non-zero exit)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_cds_build_oracle", "label": "cds build --production \u2014 the only real oracle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CAP's own compiler is the only thing that knows what CAP accepts; the first run found five defects nothing else could see, including a CDS type that does not exist."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_check_emitted", "label": "checks/emitted.js \u2014 scope, sentinels, re-parse", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_check_leaks", "label": "checks/leaks.js \u2014 the remaining $. surface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asks not only what is left of the $. surface but whether every remaining site sits in a file that carries a finding \u2014 a leak with a finding is honest, a leak without one is a lie."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_check_awaits", "label": "checks/awaits.js \u2014 every cross-file async call awaited", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_check_ceiling", "label": "checks/ceiling.js \u2014 what each refusal is worth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prints the chains where a given refusal code is the only blocker, so effort goes where a fix actually unblocks statements."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_measure_before_building", "label": "Measure before building", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Also: read the output of the statements a change just unblocked \u2014 a refusal hides everything downstream of it, and three real bugs were found exactly that way."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_rule_never_write_neo_tree", "target": "src_core_write_writefiles", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_never_write_neo_tree", "target": "src_core_write_isinside", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 Write", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_dry_run_default", "target": "src_core_write_writefiles", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 Write", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_ast_locates_text_edited", "target": "src_transform_js_applyedits", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_single_applyedits", "target": "src_transform_js_applyedits", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_single_applyedits", "target": "src_transform_file_transformfile", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_terminal_boundary", "target": "bin_neo2cf_main", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_rule_terminal_boundary", "target": "src_report_render_renderconvert", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_phase_intake", "target": "src_core_intake_discover", "relation": "ref